hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"177","Abu Musa told me, Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid Abu Asim told me, Sufyan told us, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of what God expiates sins with? And good deeds are added to it.” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Performing ablution thoroughly in the case of hardship, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer.” Then he mentioned Hadith. Abu Bakr said: No one narrated this news on the authority of Sufyan other than Abu Asim. If Abu Asim had memorized it, then this is a strange chain of narration. This is a long story that I have narrated in a number of chapters, and the famous one in this text is Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Saeed, not on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr. Hna Abu Musa, and Ahmad bin Abdah, Abu Musa said: us, and Ahmad said: Abu Amir told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel"
